       The  function  sseett__ffiieelldd__ttyyppee associates a field type with a given form
       field.  This is the type checked by validation functions.   Most  field
       types  are  configurable,  via arguments which the caller provides when
       calling sseett__ffiieelldd__ttyyppee.

       Several field types are predefined by the form library.

PPRREEDDEEFFIINNEEDD TTYYPPEESS
       It is possible to set up new  programmer-defined  field  types.   Field
       types  are implemented via the FFIIEELLDDTTYYPPEE data structure, which contains
       several pointers to functions.

       See the ffoorrmm__ffiieellddttyyppee(3X) manual page, which describes functions which
       can be used to construct a field-type dynamically.

       The predefined types are as follows:

